This is page 1 of a short exposé titled 'Formule de décalage (Quillen–Bousfield) [cf. Illusie]'. It sits inside notes for a 1976 IHÉS talk on the divided-power de Rham complex. The previous page treats Steenrod powers; the next treats Dold–Puppe, Dold–Thom and the weight grading on the homology of Eilenberg–MacLane spaces.

Setup. For a functor F on modules (Sym^i, Λ^i, Γ^i), L_*F(M,n) denotes the Dold–Puppe derived functor evaluated on M placed in degree n, written M[n]. The model of M[n] is the simplicial module K(M,n). Grothendieck uses the simplicial path sequence 0 → K(M,n) → E(M,n+1) → K(M,n+1) → 0, where E(M,n+1) is contractible and degreewise free when M is free.

Koszul complexes. Applying Koszul complexes to this short exact sequence degreewise gives exact resolutions:
(i) 0 → Λ^i K → Λ^{i-1}K ⊗ S^1E → … → S^iE → S^i K' → 0;
(ii) 0 → Γ^i K → Γ^{i-1}K ⊗ Λ^1E → … → Λ^iE → Λ^i K' → 0.
Here K = K(M,n) and K' = K(M,n+1). Because E is contractible, the middle terms (which involve E) contribute nothing to homology. One deduces the décalage isomorphisms:
- L Sym^i(X[1]) ≃ LΛ^i(X)[i], boxed as L_r Sym^i K(M,n+1) ≃ L_{r-i} Λ^i K(M,n);
- LΛ^i(X[1]) ≃ LΓ^i(X)[i];
- hence L Sym^i(X[2]) ≃ LΓ^i(X)[2i].

Purpose. Via Dold's theorem H_*(K(M,n)) = π_* Sym(ℤM(n)) (next page), this computes the weight-graded pieces of the homology of Eilenberg–MacLane spaces in terms of divided powers. That is presumably the bridge to the divided-power de Rham complex. The material is a faithful sketch of Illusie, Complexe cotangent I, ch. I §4.3.2, which Grothendieck explicitly cites. The fragment 'Λ^{-1}φ ⊗_ℤ M' is unclear.
